{
  "dom_id": "step-509412",
  "name": "The Number of Intersection Points",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220347/assets/b9cb25bbb7b3076a3dae8688a232d18ec4092d68d9e815dedb438bc6900d97bb.png)\n\nA line and a parabola may have **two**, \n**one**, or **no** points of intersection.\n\nThis is similar to how a quadratic equation may have  **two**, \n**one**, or **no** solutions.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at another example.",
