  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-509412\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"509412\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"13863\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-509412\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-10\">The Number of Intersection Points</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"509412\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <div id=\"graphic-62995b84b93fb7f3985af35efe5b2630\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/62995b84b93fb7f3985af35efe5b2630\"></div>\n\n\n<p>A line and a parabola may have <span style=\"color:rgb(230,159,0)\"><strong>two</strong></span>, \n<span style=\"color:rgb(69,155,118)\"><strong>one</strong></span>, or <span style=\"color:rgb(192,126,164)\"><strong>no</strong></span> points of intersection.</p>\n<p>This is similar to how a quadratic equation may have  <span style=\"color:rgb(230,159,0)\"><strong>two</strong></span>, \n<span style=\"color:rgb(69,155,118)\"><strong>one</strong></span>, or <span style=\"color:rgb(192,126,164)\"><strong>no</strong></span> solutions.</p>\n<p>With that in mind, let's look at another example.</p>\n\n        </div>",
